# Dependencies
node_modules

# Build output
.next
dist
build
out
coverage
*.tsbuildinfo

# Local databases (regenerated via db:push + seed)
*.db
*.db-journal

# Environment — never commit secrets
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Logs & OS
*.log
.DS_Store

# Editor
.idea

# Local MCP config (contains API token — never commit)
.mcp.json

# Generated Prisma clients — `prisma generate` runs at the start of every
# build, and the schema declares six binaryTargets, so these engine binaries
# are rebuilt on the server every time. Committed, they were 244MB of the
# repo's 260MB: every deploy dragged a quarter-gigabyte of regenerable
# binaries onto a shared host before it could even start installing.
**/src/generated/

# Build output is never tracked. Hostinger DOES run `npm run build` on the
# server — its build logs show `next build` completing and emitting every
# route. Committing apps/grow/.next was the cause of, not the cure for, the
# stale deploys: the checked-in build layered over the server's fresh one and
# the app ended up serving a mix of two builds.
**/.next/
